21:59.394 --> 22:09.618
[SPEAKER_00]: parakite pilot at the same time? Or are these two very different things where a human brain is only able to develop safety mechanisms for one

22:09.638 --> 22:20.364
[SPEAKER_00]: sport effectively than for two different sports and then mix and match because as I said 5% brake pressure in paragliders is nice but 5% brake

22:20.384 --> 22:28.769
[SPEAKER_00]: pressure in paragliding is freaking dangerous because you're messing up with the reflex yeah I think you can be a great pilot in both but I think

22:28.809 --> 22:40.119
[SPEAKER_00]: there goes like many more hours in becoming a good pilot under a normal paraglider it's way more It's way more advanced, I would say, compared

22:40.159 --> 22:50.722
[SPEAKER_01]: to a parakite. On a parakite, everything with flying is just so easy. And that's the thing why I told you people get so confident. And then, yeah,

